  "term": "radiculopathy",
  "definition": "Radiculopathy is a disorder affecting a spinal nerve root, often due to compression from problems such as a displaced intervertebral disk, spinal injury, or other spinal disease. It can cause nerve-root-related pain, weakness, and loss of sensation in the areas served by the affected root.",
